WEBVTT

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.640
MOLLY: Come on, Buster.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.080
ANDY'S MOM: Is that it, honey?
You got everything?

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.840
ANDY: Yeah. Just a few more boxes
in my room.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.000
Okay. Come on.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.760
That's enough. That's enough.
That's enough!

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.760
All right. Go. Go, go!

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.440
Okay. All clear.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.440
Oh!

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.440
Oh, there you are.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.920
(CHUCKLING)

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.760
-BUZZ: There you go.
-Buzz.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.120
-This isn't goodbye.
-Hey, Woody. Have fun at college.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.040
Yeah, but not too much fun.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.520
(CHUCKLING)

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.280
-Woody, take care of Andy.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.960
He's a good kid.
Tell him to get a haircut.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:04.880
Sure thing.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.880
Jessie, you'll be okay in the attic?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.360
'Course I will. Besides, I know about

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.040
-Buzz's Spanish mode.
-My what?

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.880
ANDY'S MOM: Honey, you want
some food for the road?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.400
ANDY: I'll get something on the way.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.400
You know where to find us, cowboy.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.840
Did you say goodbye to Molly?

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.920
Mom, we've said goodbye
like 10 times.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.080
(ANDY'S MOM GASPS)

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.200
Oh, Andy.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.680
Mom, it's okay.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.280
ANDY'S MOM: I know. It's just...

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.160
(SNIFFLES)

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.760
I wish I could always be with you.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.680
ANDY: You will be, Mom.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.200
Hey, aren't you gonna say goodbye
to Buster?

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.440
Of course I am. Who's a good doggy?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.400
Who's a good doggy? I'm gonna
miss you. I'm gonna miss you.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.360
(MOLLY LAUGHING)

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.400
ANDY: I'm gonna miss you.
ANDY'S MOM: Don't, Andy.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.120
MOLLY: Good boy.
He's telling you to go already.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.640
ANDY'S MOM: Come on.
Get the rest of your things.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.240
Okay, Buster.
Now don't let Molly near my stuff.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.800
(CHUCKLING) Hey.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.760
Hey, Mom! So, you really think
I should donate these?

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.080
ANDY'S MOM: It's up to you, honey.
Whatever you wanna do.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.440
"Don't go in there!
The bakery is haunted!"

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.120
(SHUSHES) "Are you crazy?
You'll wake up all the ghosts."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.640
"Look out!
The ghosts are throwing pies!"

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.440
Splat! Splat! Splat!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.240
Mom.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.560
-Andy?
-Hi.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.240
BONNIE'S MOM: Wow. Look at you.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.400
Well, I hear you're off to college.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.320
Yeah. Right now, actually.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.560
So, what can we do for you?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.800
Uh, I have some toys here.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.800
BONNIE'S MOM:
Ooh. You hear that, Bonnie?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.480
So, you're Bonnie?

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.840
I'm Andy.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.640
Someone told me
you're really good with toys.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.640
These are mine,
but I'm going away now,

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.720
so I need someone really special
to play with them.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.160
This is Jessie, the roughest,
toughest cowgirl in the whole West.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.680
She loves critters, but none more
than her best pal, Bullseye.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.320
(MIMICS NEIGHING HORSE)

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.720
Yee-haw!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.840
Here.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.080
This is Rex, the meanest, most
terrifying dinosaur who ever lived!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.280
(MIMICS ROARING)

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.080
The Potato Heads. Mr. and Mrs.
You gotta keep 'em together,

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.360
'cause they're madly in love.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:16.440
Now Slinky here is
as loyal as any dog you could want.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.320
And Hamm,
he'll keep your money safe,

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.640
but he's also one of the most dastardly
villains of all time, evil Dr. Pork Chop.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.840
These little dudes
are from a strange alien world.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.600
Pizza Planet.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.560
And this

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.880
(MIMICS WHOOSHING)

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.320
is Buzz Lightyear, the coolest toy ever!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.480
Look, he can fly and shoot lasers!

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.240
He's sworn to protect the galaxy
from the evil Emperor Zurg.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.560
VOICE BOX: To infinity and beyond!

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.720
Now, you gotta promise
to take good care of these guys.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.520
They mean a lot to me.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.760
My cowboy!

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.760
Woody? What's he doing in there?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.560
-"There's a snake in my boot."
-Wha...?

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.720
VOICE BOX:
There's a snake in my boot.

